Execute the current notebook final UI cells in a clean child process on oec-1 / phase2_3d. The A100 acceptance must run the actual FLUX final cell and call /generate, run the TRELLIS-only final cell and call /generate_3d with GLB geometry reopen, and start the combined notebook's TRELLIS final cell to validate its app-level theme and UI launch. Use the existing inference lock and cache-only offline mode. No package installs, model downloads, shared output writes, cache purge, QA mutation, storage-reserve access or arbitrary process termination. Artifacts must contain child logs, machine-readable reports, a verified FLUX image and a TRELLIS GLB.
The default-port regression now also verifies the environment override used to avoid port collisions in the live cell acceptance harness.
The legacy tunnel-port test now checks the default 7862 and environment-configurable port variable instead of requiring a hard-coded server_port argument.

Harness correction: the parent validation process now derives the exact same run-scoped FLUX scratch directory used by the child process, rather than trying to read a child-only environment variable. Rerun the live final-cell acceptance and verify the PNG/metadata artifact.
The last exact-cell A100 test passed FLUX final-cell generation/PNG validation but exposed that the TRELLIS final cell assumed an earlier setup cell had already placed the checked-out TRELLIS.2 source root on sys.path. Both TRELLIS notebook cells now resolve the existing SYSTEM_DIRS["models"]/TRELLIS.2 source root read-only, require trellis2/pipelines to exist, and fail with an actionable message rather than installing or downloading anything. Re-run all three exact-cell stages on oec-1.
The last live attempt reached the TRELLIS-only /generate_3d route but gradio_client rejected a raw input path as an ImageData payload. The harness now wraps the local test image using the supported gradio_client.handle_file helper before calling /generate_3d; this is test input serialization, not a model/notebook code change. Re-run the exact final-cell acceptance.

The combined notebook's separate FLUX service-start cell was previously not part of runtime acceptance and its default Conda root pointed at OEC/Conda instead of the service manager's ~/Conda default. The cell now uses the manager-consistent default with an actionable check. Also launch this actual combined-notebook FLUX cell on an available GPU and unique port, call its /generate API in local scratch, validate the PNG/sidecar, and stop the service only if this acceptance run started it. Do not stop or alter any pre-existing managed service.
